<Layout title="Privacy — Backplane" description="Privacy information for Backplane and connected services.">
  <main class="legal-document-page">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>Backplane is open-source software. When you run it locally, session data and settings stay in the environments and storage you configure.</p>
    <p>Optional services, including T3 Connect, are operated by their respective providers and have their own privacy policies. Review those policies before connecting an account or sending data through a hosted service.</p>
    <p><a href="/privacy-policy">Backplane privacy information</a></p>
    <p>For the source license, see the <a href="https://github.com/i2cjak/Backplane/blob/t3cad/LICENSE" rel="noopener noreferrer">Backplane MIT license</a>.</p>
  </main>
</Layout>
